From: Port of Gdynia Authority - Compliance Desk <compliance@portgdynia-authority.example>
To: undisclosed-recipients:;
Date: Thu, 14 Mar 2024 11:02:44 +0100
Subject: Notice ZMPG/OS/2024/0317 to port tenants and operators of refrigerated cargo yards: environmental and safety requirements applicable from 1 July 2024
X-Mailer: PortNotify 3.2

Dear Sir or Madam,

Pursuant to the port regulations of 19 December 2023 (Harbour Master's Order no. 14/2023, section 6) and the decision of the Port Environmental Committee of 29 February 2024, we hereby notify all tenants and operators who run refrigerated cargo yards within the port boundary of the following requirements, which take effect on 1 July 2024 unless stated otherwise below. Please note that this notice replaces our earlier circular ZMPG/OS/2022/0088 of 6 June 2022, the contents of which are no longer valid.

1. Refrigerant register. Every fixed refrigeration unit containing 3 kg or more of fluorinated refrigerant and operated in the port area, including units mounted on containers while they are on the premises of a tenant for more than 72 hours, shall be entered in the Port Environmental Register (PER) by 30 June 2024. Registration is made electronically on the PER portal. The fee is 190 PLN per site per year, due on registration. Each entry shall state the serial number, the refrigerant designation, the nominal charge in kilograms, the date of the last leak check and the name of the person responsible.

2. Logbook. A logbook shall be kept for each registered unit and shall remain at the site where the unit is located. It shall record any refrigerant added, any leak found, and each leak check. Logbooks shall be retained for 5 years.

3. Leak checks. The frequency of leak checks depends on the nominal charge of the unit: from 3 kg up to and including 29 kg, once every 12 months; from 30 kg up to and including 299 kg, once every 6 months; 300 kg and above, once every 3 months. The check shall be carried out by a person holding a refrigerant handling certificate of category I or II recognised in the port area. If a leak is found, it shall be repaired within 14 days and the unit shall be checked again within 30 days after the repair. The annual leakage rate of a tenant's total registered charge shall not exceed 5 per cent; a tenant exceeding that figure shall submit a remediation plan within 45 days of the end of the calendar year.

4. Shore power and pedestals. Electrical pedestals supplying refrigerated containers shall be inspected by a qualified person at least every 12 months, including a thermographic scan under load of not less than 70 per cent of the rated current. The inspection certificate shall be held on site and presented on request. Pedestals found with a surface temperature rise of more than 40 K above ambient shall be taken out of use immediately.

5. Noise. The equivalent sound level at the tenant's boundary shall not exceed 60 dB(A) between 06:00 and 22:00 and 50 dB(A) between 22:00 and 06:00. The port will carry out a measurement campaign between 8 and 12 April 2024 at boundaries adjoining residential areas. Tenants whose result exceeds a limit by more than 3 dB(A) shall submit a noise reduction plan within 30 days of notification of the result.

6. Incident reporting. Any spill of more than 20 litres of fuel or oil, and any release of 2 kg or more of refrigerant, shall be reported to port control by telephone (+48 58 555 0162, 24 hours) within 4 hours of its discovery and in writing within 3 working days.

7. Inspection and penalties. Inspectors of the Port Compliance Desk may inspect yards without notice from 15 April 2024. A breach of this notice is punishable by an administrative fine of between 2,000 PLN and 25,000 PLN per breach; repeated breaches within 12 months double the range. Appeals against a fine can be lodged within 14 days of delivery with the Harbour Master.

8. Acknowledgement. Tenants shall inform the Compliance Desk, not later than 12 April 2024, of the name, telephone number and e-mail address of the person responsible for environmental compliance. Please reply to this message or write to compliance@portgdynia-authority.example, quoting the reference ZMPG/OS/2024/0317.

An information session for tenants will take place on 21 March 2024 at 10:00 in the Harbour Master's building, Hall B (registration not required). Presentation slides will be published on the PER portal afterwards.

Yours faithfully,

Ewa Kłosińska-Dahl
Head of the Compliance Desk
Port of Gdynia Authority
